ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to activate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something start working"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to activate your number so you can make and receive calls."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you may use when talking about setting up a meeting. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mailbox"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a system for managing telephone messages"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You haven't set up your voice mailbox."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to blink"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go on and off quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wondered why the light on the answering machine never blinked."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pick up the pace "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go faster"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You're going to have to pick up the pace."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall behind"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become less successful than other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You don't want to be falling behind, do you?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "turn up nothing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to find nothing even when searching for it thoroughly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My research has turned up nothing!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "redundant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "exceeding what is usual or necessary"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It seems redundant to leave a message as well."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "around the block "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have had a lot of experience with something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As someone who has been around the block a few times, I suggest you leave him a message."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le12ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect with Past Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You often use the<span class=\"italic\"> Present Perfect </span>with other tenses in the same sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"italic\">Present Perfect</span> with past tenses to:<br/><br/>  1. describe states or events that have continued since a time in the past. You use the words <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ever since</span> etc.<br/><br/> For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">He'<span class=\"strong\">s been</span> a bit more careful about his diet <span class=\"strong\">since he went</span> to the doctor's.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Ever since</span> I first <span class=\"strong\">saw</span> her, I'<span class=\"strong\">ve been thinking</span> about her all the time.</span><br/><br/>  2. describe long-term or repeated feelings and thoughts about past events. <br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'<span class=\"strong\">ve often thought</span> about why he <span class=\"strong\">decided</span> to become an astronaut.<br/> I'<span class=\"strong\">ve always felt</span> I <span class=\"strong\">did</span> the wrong thing when I took that job.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">ve wondered</span> why my phone never <span class=\"strong\">blinked</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">started</span> late as I'<span class=\"strong\">ve felt</span> a bit under the weather."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">sent</span> him an e-mail since I <span class=\"strong\">haven't spoken</span> to him at all."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Future Perfect Continuous: Stating the Cause of Something in the Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect Continuous</span> before another action in the future to show <span class=\"underline\">cause </span>and <span class=\"underline\">effect</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Jason will be tired when he gets home because he<span class=\"strong\"> will have been running</span> for over an hour.</span><br/><br/>  In this example, the cause of Jason being tired is that he will have been running for a long time. You use this tense to project yourself into the future and look back on events leading up to that point.<br/><br/>  The form of the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect Continuous </span>tense is:<br/><br/>  subject + will have been + v-ing"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You<span class=\"strong\"> will have been working </span>with BFP for a month next week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will be finished because I <span class=\"strong\">will have been working </span>for 12 hours before I head home."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'll be tired because you<span class=\"strong\"> will have been travelling</span> 4 hours by the time you get back to Boston."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of someone you know who has been working in a certain industry for a long time. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down 10 questions you can ask them. Think of questions where the answer will start with <span class=\"italic\">I will have been verb +ing \u2026 </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Set up an interview with this professional and ask them your questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down their answers. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use all the answers to write a paragraph about them."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I come up with questions to ask about the progress of actions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about events related to work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I summarize information gathered from an interview."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le12ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le12ob03re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le12ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Adam Bari here.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Hello Adam. This is Boris.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Hello, Mr. Brody.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Mr. Bari, you will have been working with BFP for a month next week. Yet, you still haven't activated your mailbox.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I'll get that sorted out. I've wondered why my phone never blinked. How is Chicago?<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Good.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le12ob03re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: You'll be tired because you will have been travelling 4 hours by the time you get back to Boston.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Yes, Mr. Bari. On to more important matters, have you completed your assignment?<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: No. I have been working on it since yesterday. I started late as I've felt a bit under the weather.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: You'll need to pick up the pace. You don't want to be falling behind, do you?<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: No, Mr. Brody. I will be finished because I will have worked for 12 hours before I head home. I've tried to set up a meeting with the author since my research turned up nothing.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: You need to get on that right away. Mr. Duncan is a busy man.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I understand. I sent him an e-mail since I've haven't spoken to him at all.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Have you called his office?", "id": 2, "time": "18000", "image": "engenn10le12ob03re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I called a few times but no one has picked up.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Did you leave a message?<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: No I assumed that if someone was there, they would have picked up.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: The correct thing to do would be to leave a voicemail message.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I sent him an e-mail. It seems redundant to leave a message as well.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: I'll have been working in this industry 10 years next month. As someone who's been around the block a few times, 